## Contributing

ferrigura is checked against upstream Mermaid at a pinned commit: every parser change against Mermaid's parser on every input, every renderer change against Mermaid's geometry in Chromium. [docs/DEVELOPING.md](./docs/DEVELOPING.md) has the setup and the commands, and [AGENTS.md](./AGENTS.md) the rules every change follows. Commit messages follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/); releases are made from them.

## License and credits

MIT, see [LICENSE](./LICENSE). Some crates port code or bundle fonts under the licenses of their sources, which their `NOTICE.md` files list; `ferrigura-elk` is under EPL-2.0. ferrigura is a port of [Mermaid](https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid), which was created by Knut Sveidqvist and is maintained by the Mermaid contributors; its license and copyright notice stay with the port.
